\ A loop whose call is the last action of a `locals` block nested in the
\ word's own block. The outer locals are not used after the inner block, so
\ they are off the stack by then and the call runs in the caller's frame.
: count
  (forall ρ; ρ n:Int^many acc:Int^many -- ρ r:Int^many)
  locals { n acc } {
    n 0 prim =
    [ acc ]
    [ n 1 prim - locals { m } { m acc 1 prim + count } ]
    if };

\ An outer local used inside the inner block and again after it is kept
\ for that later use: n + acc, then + acc again.
: add-twice
  (forall ρ; ρ n:Int^many acc:Int^many -- ρ r:Int^many)
  locals { n acc } { n locals { m } { m acc prim + } acc prim + };

\ The later `acc` is bound again by its own block, so it is not the outer
\ one: 2 + 3, then 5 + 10.
: shadowed
  (forall ρ; ρ n:Int^many acc:Int^many -- ρ r:Int^many)
  locals { n acc } { n locals { m } { m acc prim + } 10 locals { acc } { acc prim + } };
